 34SI dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 03-Jun-2025)          
 34SI c  Multi-nucleon transfer and deep-inelastic binary grazing reactions.    
 34SI c  2010WaZT,2010Wa20: A 215-MeV {+36}S{+9+} beam was produced from the    
 34SI2c  XTU-Tandem ALPI-superconducting linear accelerator complex at the INFN 
 34SI3c  Legnaro National Laboratory, Italy. The target was 300-|mg/cm{+2},     
 34SI4c  99.7% enriched {+208}Pb on a 20-|mg/cm{+2} carbon backing.             
 34SI5c  Projectile-like fragments produced in binary grazing reactions were    
 34SI6c  separated and identified by the PRISMA spectrometer. |g rays were      
 34SI7c  detected using the CLARA array of 22 escape-suppressed Ge clover       
 34SI8c  detectors covering the azimuthal angles from 98|' to 180|'. Measured   
 34SI9c  E|g with Doppler corrections, I|g, and ({+34}Si)|g-coin. Deduced       
 34SIAc  levels. Compared with shell-model calculations.                        
